A system prevents deadlock by resource ordering. Each of the five mutexes A, B, C, D, E gets a distinct rank, and the rule is: a thread may lock mutex m only if rank(m) is **greater than the rank of every mutex it currently holds**.

The threads below must run unchanged:

```c
/* T1 */ lock(A); lock(C); unlock(C); lock(B); unlock(B); unlock(A);
/* T2 */ lock(B); lock(D); unlock(D); unlock(B);
/* T3 */ lock(C); lock(E); unlock(E); unlock(C);
/* T4 */ lock(E); unlock(E); lock(D); unlock(D); lock(A); unlock(A);
```

How many of the 5! = 120 possible rank assignments let all four threads run without ever breaking the rule?
